<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander of Battenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1893">1893</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Alexander I of Bulgaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander of Battenberg was a German prince elected the first ruler of the autonomous Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 1879. He accepted the union with Eastern Rumelia in 1885 and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> at Slivnitsa that year, but his independence angered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>; pro-Russian officers forced his abdication in 1886.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-of-battenberg.jpg" alt="Alexander of Battenberg" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitar Karastoyanov · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_I_of_Bulgaria_by_Dimitar_Karastoyanov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
